dist
.angular

# Per-example lockfiles, created by running `npm install` inside an example folder. Only the
# shared framework-level lockfile is tracked. See the explanation in /examples/README.md.
#
# Ignore every lockfile under `examples/`, then re-include the shared framework-level ones --
# the only lockfiles that sit at exactly `<version>/<category>/<framework>/`. Written as a pair
# so a new framework or category directory needs no edit here: the install globs accept any
# `angular-*` and `vue*` name, and a name with no rule puts its leaf lockfiles back within
# reach of the release job's bare `git add .`.
**/package-lock.json
!*/*/*/package-lock.json
